lklfuse: on Darwin, Mac xattrs are user.N, or kept in netatalk's or Samba's scheme where the volume already uses one

Linux takes only namespaced xattr names, so a Mac name such as com.apple.FinderInfo or
com.apple.metadata:_kMDItemUserTags failed (EPERM through macFUSE; the census, push A, saw Finder tags and labels lost
on ext4, btrfs, xfs and f2fs), and with noappledouble nothing caught it. On Darwin a Mac name N is now stored as the
Linux name user.N, always: names with no dot, names already starting with user., and names like security.foo too. Linux
user.X is shown to the Mac as X; Linux's other namespaces (security, trusted, system, POSIX ACLs) are neither shown nor
writable, so nothing can clash. On apfs the prefix is osx., the namespace the Linux driver puts every name macOS wrote
in, so a Mac reads macOS's own names there.

One legacy scheme: before this, linuxfs passed Mac names through, and on NTFS (ntfs3 takes any name) they were kept
bare; the census saw Finder tags round-trip there. A bare com.apple.* name is shown under its own name, and read and
changed where it is; a new name still goes to user.N; a name there both ways is listed once, and is its user.N copy.
Every other name outside user. (WSL's $LXUID and the like among them) stays hidden.

Volumes that netatalk or Samba (vfs_fruit) have served keep a Mac file's metadata their own ways (netatalk 4.6.1's and
Samba 4.25.1's sources, recorded in the item's findings):
- netatalk, and Samba's fruit:metadata=netatalk: the Finder Info is 32 bytes of an AppleDouble blob,
  user.org.netatalk.Metadata (402 bytes in netatalk's layout, Finder Info at 122), and other xattrs are user.N;
- Samba's fruit:metadata=stream over streams_xattr: the Finder Info is 32 bytes at 16 of the AFP_AfpInfo stream (60
  bytes), the resource fork the AFP_Resource stream, and every other xattr a stream named as the Mac's SMB client names
  it (':' and the other characters NTFS refuses as U+F001-U+F027); a stream is the xattr user.DosStream.NAME:$DATA,
  holding its data and one more byte, 0. (netatalk's resource fork xattr, user.org.netatalk.ResourceFork, is read as
  com.apple.ResourceFork too.)
A file's attribute is read where it is and changed there. A new one goes in the file's own scheme (the carriers it has
already), else the volume's, chosen once at mount: netatalk's if the root has .AppleDB, .AppleDouble or .AppleDesktop or
a netatalk blob is on the root or one of its first 32 entries, else fruit's if a stream is, else user.N. The carriers
are never listed by their own names, only as the attributes they carry, and cannot be written by them (EPERM). Inside a
blob or an AfpInfo only the Finder Info's 32 bytes are ever written; one that is malformed (too short, a wrong magic, a
stream in extents) is neither read (ENOATTR) nor written (EIO), so another server's data is never damaged. As on HFS+:
an all-zero Finder Info in a blob or an AfpInfo is no Finder Info (removing it zeroes it in the blob, which keeps
netatalk's other data, and removes the AfpInfo, as Samba does); a Finder Info is 32 bytes (ERANGE otherwise); and a value
the filesystem cannot hold is refused with ENOSPC, the only refusal HFS+ gave (it took 64 MiB + 1; linuxfs gave E2BIG
at 128 KiB). tests/lklfuse-ops-test.c checks the name table, the choice of scheme, and each scheme's round trip, on four
images tests/lib/xattr-images.sh makes, one per scheme and one mixing them, and the legacy scheme on a blank NTFS
image, with the raw names and bytes as Linux sees them.

Darwin only: on Linux the names are passed as given, as before.

diff -ru a/tools/lkl/lklfuse.c b/tools/lkl/lklfuse.c
--- a/tools/lkl/lklfuse.c
+++ b/tools/lkl/lklfuse.c
@@ -139,6 +139,8 @@
 
 /* LKL's PATH_MAX, for the paths lklfuse rewrites (Darwin's own PATH_MAX is 1024) */
 #define LKLFUSE_PATH_MAX 4096
+#define LKLFUSE_FINDERINFO "com.apple.FinderInfo"
+#define LKLFUSE_FINDERINFO_LEN 32
 
 #ifdef __APPLE__
 #include <sys/xattr.h>
@@ -773,9 +775,655 @@
 {
 	return fuse_new(args, ops, size, data);
 }
+
+/*
+ * Mac xattrs (spec: item 7). Linux takes only namespaced names, so a Mac name N is stored as the Linux name user.N,
+ * always (on apfs, osx.N: macOS's own names, as the Linux driver shows them). Linux user.X is shown to the Mac as X;
+ * Linux's other namespaces (security, trusted, system) are neither shown nor writable, so nothing can clash. One legacy
+ * scheme: before this, linuxfs passed Mac names through, and NTFS (whose ntfs3 takes any name) kept them bare. A bare
+ * com.apple.* name is shown as itself and read and changed where it is; a new one is still user.N, and a name there
+ * both ways is its user.N. Every other name outside user. (WSL's $LX* among them) stays hidden. Volumes
+ * netatalk or Samba (vfs_fruit) have served keep a Mac file's metadata their own ways (item-7-findings.md has the
+ * encodings, from their sources):
+ * - netatalk, and fruit:metadata=netatalk: the Finder Info is 32 bytes of an AppleDouble blob, user.org.netatalk.Metadata
+ *   (402 bytes, Finder Info at 122, in netatalk's own layout), and the file's other xattrs are user.N, as ours;
+ * - fruit:metadata=stream, over streams_xattr: the Finder Info is 32 bytes at 16 of the AFP_AfpInfo stream (60 bytes),
+ *   the resource fork the AFP_Resource stream, and every other xattr a stream named as the Mac's SMB client names it (the
+ *   characters NTFS refuses, ':' among them, in the Unicode private range); a stream is the xattr
+ *   user.DosStream.NAME:$DATA, its data and one more byte, 0 (an extent count otherwise).
+ * A file's attribute is read where it is and changed there; a new one goes in the file's own scheme (the carriers it
+ * already has), else the volume's, chosen once at mount from netatalk's root directories or the carriers on the root
+ * and its first 32 entries. Carriers are never shown by their own names, only as the attributes they carry. Inside a
+ * blob or AfpInfo only the Finder Info's 32 bytes are ever written, and one that is malformed is neither read (ENOATTR)
+ * nor written (EIO), so another server's data is never damaged. As on HFS+, an all-zero Finder Info there is none, a
+ * Finder Info is 32 bytes (ERANGE otherwise), and a value the filesystem cannot hold is refused with ENOSPC, the only
+ * refusal HFS+ gave (item-7-findings.md, push C).
+ */
+enum lklfuse_xscheme { XS_OURS, XS_NETATALK, XS_FRUIT_STREAM };
+static const char *lklfuse_xpre = "user.";	/* the Linux namespace Mac names live in */
+static enum lklfuse_xscheme lklfuse_xs_vol;	/* the volume's scheme, for new attributes */
+
+#define LKLFUSE_XCREATE 1	/* Linux's XATTR_CREATE and XATTR_REPLACE */
+#define LKLFUSE_XREPLACE 2
+#define LKLFUSE_XNAME_MAX 512	/* a Linux xattr name lklfuse builds (Linux's own limit is 255) */
+#define LKLFUSE_XVAL_MAX 65536	/* Linux's XATTR_SIZE_MAX: no carrier is larger */
+#define LKLFUSE_RESOURCEFORK "com.apple.ResourceFork"
+#define LKLFUSE_XLEGACY "com.apple."	/* the bare names linuxfs kept on NTFS before user.N */
+#define LKLFUSE_XMETA "org.netatalk.Metadata"
+#define LKLFUSE_XRSRC "org.netatalk.ResourceFork"
+#define LKLFUSE_XSTREAM "DosStream."
+#define LKLFUSE_XSTREAM_EXT "DosStreamExt."
+#define LKLFUSE_XSTREAM_TYPE ":$DATA"
+#define LKLFUSE_XAFPINFO "AFP_AfpInfo"
+#define LKLFUSE_XAFPRSRC "AFP_Resource"
+#define LKLFUSE_AD_MAGIC 0x00051607	/* AppleDouble */
+#define LKLFUSE_AD_VERSION 0x00020000
+#define LKLFUSE_AD_LEN 402	/* netatalk's AD_DATASZ_EA */
+#define LKLFUSE_AD_FINDERI 122
+#define LKLFUSE_AFPINFO_LEN 60	/* AFP_INFO_SIZE */
+#define LKLFUSE_AFPINFO_FINDERI 16
+#define LKLFUSE_AFP_SIGNATURE 0x41465000
+#define LKLFUSE_AFP_VERSION 0x00000100
+#define LKLFUSE_AD_DATE_DELTA 946684800	/* AppleDouble dates count from 2000 */
+
+/* the characters the Mac's SMB client sends as U+F001 to U+F027, in that order (Samba's macos_string_replace_map) */
+static const char lklfuse_xpriv[] = "\x01\x02\x03\x04\x05\x06\x07\x08\x09\x0a\x0b\x0c\x0d\x0e\x0f\x10\x11\x12\x13\x14"
+				    "\x15\x16\x17\x18\x19\x1a\x1b\x1c\x1d\x1e\x1f\"*:<>?\\|";
+
+static const char *lklfuse_xpre_for(const char *type)
+{
+	return type && strcmp(type, "apfs") == 0 ? "osx." : "user.";
+}
+
+static unsigned int lklfuse_be32(const void *p)
+{
+	const unsigned char *u = p;
+
+	return (unsigned int)u[0] << 24 | u[1] << 16 | u[2] << 8 | u[3];
+}
+
+static void lklfuse_put_be32(void *p, unsigned int v)
+{
+	unsigned char *u = p;
+
+	u[0] = v >> 24;
+	u[1] = v >> 16;
+	u[2] = v >> 8;
+	u[3] = v;
+}
+
+static int lklfuse_xzero(const char *p, size_t n)
+{
+	while (n--)
+		if (*p++)
+			return 0;
+	return 1;
+}
+
+/* X, a name past the prefix, is another scheme's carrier */
+static int lklfuse_xcarrier(const char *x)
+{
+	return strcmp(x, LKLFUSE_XMETA) == 0 || strcmp(x, LKLFUSE_XRSRC) == 0 ||
+	       strncmp(x, LKLFUSE_XSTREAM, sizeof(LKLFUSE_XSTREAM) - 1) == 0 ||
+	       strncmp(x, LKLFUSE_XSTREAM_EXT, sizeof(LKLFUSE_XSTREAM_EXT) - 1) == 0;
+}
+
+/* Mac name N: user.N, always */
+static int lklfuse_xname_to_linux(const char *mac, char *out, size_t len)
+{
+	int n = snprintf(out, len, "%s%s", lklfuse_xpre, mac);
+
+	return n < 0 || (size_t)n >= len ? -ENAMETOOLONG : 0;
+}
+
+/* Linux name user.X: X (0), and a legacy bare com.apple.X itself; 1 for every other name and every carrier, hidden */
+static int lklfuse_xname_to_mac(const char *lname, char *out, size_t len)
+{
+	size_t n = strlen(lklfuse_xpre);
+
+	if (strncmp(lname, LKLFUSE_XLEGACY, sizeof(LKLFUSE_XLEGACY) - 1) == 0 && lname[sizeof(LKLFUSE_XLEGACY) - 1])
+		n = 0;
+	else if (strncmp(lname, lklfuse_xpre, n) || !lname[n] || lklfuse_xcarrier(lname + n))
+		return 1;
+	if (strlen(lname + n) >= len)
+		return -ERANGE;
+	strcpy(out, lname + n);
+	return 0;
+}
+
+/* Mac name MAC may be stored under its own name: not one that is a carrier's */
+static int lklfuse_xmac_ok(const char *mac)
+{
+	char l[LKLFUSE_XNAME_MAX], m[LKLFUSE_XNAME_MAX];
+
+	return lklfuse_xname_to_linux(mac, l, sizeof(l)) == 0 && lklfuse_xname_to_mac(l, m, sizeof(m)) == 0;
+}
+
+/* Linux xattr NAME of PATH, whole, into *val (malloc'd; the caller frees it): its length, or a negative LKL error */
+static long lklfuse_xread(const char *path, const char *name, char **val)
+{
+	long n = lkl_sys_getxattr(path, name, NULL, 0), m;
+
+	*val = NULL;
+	if (n < 0)
+		return n;
+	if (n > LKLFUSE_XVAL_MAX)
+		return -LKL_E2BIG;
+	*val = malloc(n ? n : 1);
+	if (!*val)
+		return -LKL_ENOMEM;
+	m = lkl_sys_getxattr(path, name, *val, n);
+	if (m < 0) {
+		free(*val);
+		*val = NULL;
+	}
+	return m;
+}
+
+/* netatalk's metadata blob VAL (LEN bytes): its Finder Info's 32 bytes, or NULL when it is not one */
+static char *lklfuse_ad_finderinfo(char *val, long len)
+{
+	unsigned int n, i, off, elen;
+	const char *e;
+
+	if (len < 26 || lklfuse_be32(val) != LKLFUSE_AD_MAGIC || lklfuse_be32(val + 4) != LKLFUSE_AD_VERSION)
+		return NULL;
+	n = (unsigned char)val[24] << 8 | (unsigned char)val[25];
+	if (26 + 12L * n > len)
+		return NULL;
+	for (i = 0, e = val + 26; i < n; i++, e += 12) {
+		if (lklfuse_be32(e) != 9)	/* ADEID_FINDERI */
+			continue;
+		off = lklfuse_be32(e + 4);
+		elen = lklfuse_be32(e + 8);
+		return elen >= LKLFUSE_FINDERINFO_LEN && off <= len && LKLFUSE_FINDERINFO_LEN <= len - off ? val + off : NULL;
+	}
+	return NULL;
+}
+
+/* AFP_AfpInfo's xattr VAL (LEN bytes): its Finder Info's 32 bytes, or NULL when it is not one */
+static char *lklfuse_afp_finderinfo(char *val, long len)
+{
+	if (len != LKLFUSE_AFPINFO_LEN + 1 || val[LKLFUSE_AFPINFO_LEN] || lklfuse_be32(val) != LKLFUSE_AFP_SIGNATURE ||
+	    lklfuse_be32(val + 4) != LKLFUSE_AFP_VERSION)
+		return NULL;
+	return val + LKLFUSE_AFPINFO_FINDERI;
+}
+
+/* the stream name the Mac's SMB client gives MAC, with the private-range characters (PRIV) or as it is */
+static int lklfuse_xstream_name(const char *mac, int priv, int typed, char *out, size_t len)
+{
+	size_t o = snprintf(out, len, "%s%s", lklfuse_xpre, LKLFUSE_XSTREAM);
+	const char *c;
+
+	if (o >= len)
+		return -ENAMETOOLONG;
+	for (; *mac; mac++) {
+		if (o + 4 > len)
+			return -ENAMETOOLONG;
+		c = priv ? strchr(lklfuse_xpriv, *mac) : NULL;
+		if (c) {
+			out[o++] = (char)0xef;
+			out[o++] = (char)0x80;
+			out[o++] = (char)(0x80 | (1 + (c - lklfuse_xpriv)));
+		} else {
+			out[o++] = *mac;
+		}
+	}
+	out[o] = '\0';
+	if (typed && o + sizeof(LKLFUSE_XSTREAM_TYPE) > len)
+		return -ENAMETOOLONG;
+	if (typed)
+		strcat(out, LKLFUSE_XSTREAM_TYPE);
+	return 0;
+}
+
+/* stream X (past user.DosStream.): the Mac name it carries, its private-range characters back as they were */
+static int lklfuse_xstream_mac(const char *x, char *out, size_t len)
+{
+	size_t n = strlen(x), o = 0;
+
+	if (n > sizeof(LKLFUSE_XSTREAM_TYPE) - 1 && strcmp(x + n - (sizeof(LKLFUSE_XSTREAM_TYPE) - 1), LKLFUSE_XSTREAM_TYPE) == 0)
+		n -= sizeof(LKLFUSE_XSTREAM_TYPE) - 1;
+	if (n == 0)
+		return -1;
+	while (n) {
+		if (o + 1 >= len)
+			return -1;
+		if (n >= 3 && (unsigned char)x[0] == 0xef && (unsigned char)x[1] == 0x80 && (unsigned char)x[2] >= 0x81 &&
+		    (unsigned char)x[2] < 0x81 + sizeof(lklfuse_xpriv) - 1) {
+			out[o++] = lklfuse_xpriv[(unsigned char)x[2] - 0x81];
+			x += 3;
+			n -= 3;
+		} else {
+			out[o++] = *x++;
+			n--;
+		}
+	}
+	out[o] = '\0';
+	if (strcmp(out, LKLFUSE_XAFPINFO) == 0)
+		strcpy(out, LKLFUSE_FINDERINFO);
+	else if (strcmp(out, LKLFUSE_XAFPRSRC) == 0)
+		strcpy(out, LKLFUSE_RESOURCEFORK);
+	return 0;
+}
+
+/* where a Mac attribute is now: the Linux xattr NAME, and for the carriers inside one, its value and the bytes the Mac sees */
+enum lklfuse_xloc { XL_NONE, XL_USER, XL_RSRC, XL_BLOB, XL_AFPINFO, XL_STREAM };	/* XL_USER: user.N, or legacy bare N */
+struct lklfuse_xat {
+	enum lklfuse_xloc loc;
+	char name[LKLFUSE_XNAME_MAX];
+	char *val;	/* XL_BLOB, XL_AFPINFO, XL_STREAM: the xattr's whole value (malloc'd) */
+	long len;
+	char *data;	/* the Mac's bytes in val (NULL: malformed, never read nor written) */
+	long dlen;
+};
+
+/* tries carrier NAME of PATH for LOC: 1 when it is there (AT filled in), 0 when not, or a negative LKL error */
+static long lklfuse_xtry(const char *path, const char *name, enum lklfuse_xloc loc, struct lklfuse_xat *at)
+{
+	long n = lklfuse_xread(path, name, &at->val);
+
+	if (n == -LKL_ENODATA)
+		return 0;
+	if (n < 0 && n != -LKL_E2BIG)
+		return n;
+	at->loc = loc;
+	at->len = n;
+	snprintf(at->name, sizeof(at->name), "%s", name);
+	if (n < 0)
+		at->data = NULL;
+	else if (loc == XL_BLOB)
+		at->data = lklfuse_ad_finderinfo(at->val, n);
+	else if (loc == XL_AFPINFO)
+		at->data = lklfuse_afp_finderinfo(at->val, n);
+	else
+		at->data = n >= 1 && at->val[n - 1] == 0 ? at->val : NULL;	/* one xattr, no extents */
+	at->dlen = loc == XL_STREAM ? n - 1 : LKLFUSE_FINDERINFO_LEN;
+	return 1;
+}
+
+/* where Mac attribute MAC of PATH is (at->loc XL_NONE when nowhere): 0, or a negative LKL error */
+static long lklfuse_xfind(const char *path, const char *mac, struct lklfuse_xat *at)
+{
+	int fi = strcmp(mac, LKLFUSE_FINDERINFO) == 0, rf = strcmp(mac, LKLFUSE_RESOURCEFORK) == 0;
+	char name[LKLFUSE_XNAME_MAX];
+	const char *stream = fi ? LKLFUSE_XAFPINFO : rf ? LKLFUSE_XAFPRSRC : mac;
+	int priv, typed;
+	long n;
+
+	memset(at, 0, sizeof(*at));
+	if (lklfuse_xname_to_linux(mac, at->name, sizeof(at->name)))
+		return -LKL_ERANGE;
+	n = lkl_sys_getxattr(path, at->name, NULL, 0);
+	if (n >= 0)
+		at->loc = XL_USER;
+	if (n != -LKL_ENODATA)
+		return n >= 0 ? 0 : n;
+	if (strncmp(mac, LKLFUSE_XLEGACY, sizeof(LKLFUSE_XLEGACY) - 1) == 0 && lkl_sys_getxattr(path, mac, NULL, 0) >= 0) {
+		at->loc = XL_USER;	/* legacy bare N; refused (EOPNOTSUPP) where the filesystem takes only namespaces */
+		snprintf(at->name, sizeof(at->name), "%s", mac);
+		return 0;
+	}
+	if (fi) {
+		snprintf(name, sizeof(name), "%s%s", lklfuse_xpre, LKLFUSE_XMETA);
+		if ((n = lklfuse_xtry(path, name, XL_BLOB, at)))
+			return n < 0 ? n : 0;
+	}
+	if (rf) {
+		snprintf(name, sizeof(name), "%s%s", lklfuse_xpre, LKLFUSE_XRSRC);
+		n = lkl_sys_getxattr(path, name, NULL, 0);
+		if (n >= 0) {
+			at->loc = XL_RSRC;
+			snprintf(at->name, sizeof(at->name), "%s", name);
+		}
+		if (n != -LKL_ENODATA)
+			return n >= 0 ? 0 : n;
+	}
+	if (!fi && !rf && (strcmp(mac, LKLFUSE_XAFPINFO) == 0 || strcmp(mac, LKLFUSE_XAFPRSRC) == 0))
+		return 0;	/* names fruit keeps for itself: never a stream of their own */
+	for (priv = 1; priv >= 0; priv--) {
+		if (!priv && !strpbrk(stream, lklfuse_xpriv))
+			break;	/* nothing to send in the private range: the same names again */
+		for (typed = 1; typed >= 0; typed--) {
+			if (lklfuse_xstream_name(stream, priv, typed, name, sizeof(name)))
+				return -LKL_ERANGE;
+			if ((n = lklfuse_xtry(path, name, fi ? XL_AFPINFO : XL_STREAM, at)))
+				return n < 0 ? n : 0;
+		}
+	}
+	at->loc = XL_NONE;
+	return 0;
+}
+
+/* the carriers PATH has: XS_NETATALK (a blob, whatever else), XS_FRUIT_STREAM (streams), or -1 for none */
+static int lklfuse_xmarks(const char *path, int nofollow)
+{
+	char b[4096], *raw = b;
+	size_t p = strlen(lklfuse_xpre);
+	long n, off;
+	int s = -1;
+
+	n = nofollow ? lkl_sys_llistxattr(path, NULL, 0) : lkl_sys_listxattr(path, NULL, 0);
+	if (n <= 0)
+		return -1;
+	if (n > (long)sizeof(b) && !(raw = malloc(n)))
+		return -1;
+	n = nofollow ? lkl_sys_llistxattr(path, raw, n) : lkl_sys_listxattr(path, raw, n);
+	for (off = 0; off < n && s != XS_NETATALK; off += strlen(raw + off) + 1) {
+		if (strncmp(raw + off, lklfuse_xpre, p))
+			continue;
+		if (strcmp(raw + off + p, LKLFUSE_XMETA) == 0)
+			s = XS_NETATALK;
+		else if (lklfuse_xcarrier(raw + off + p))
+			s = XS_FRUIT_STREAM;
+	}
+	if (raw != b)
+		free(raw);
+	return s;
+}
+
+/* the scheme PATH already uses: its carriers', else the volume's */
+static enum lklfuse_xscheme lklfuse_file_xscheme(const char *path)
+{
+	int s = lklfuse_xmarks(path, 0);
+
+	return s >= 0 ? (enum lklfuse_xscheme)s : lklfuse_xs_vol;
+}
+
+/* once, at mount: netatalk's root directories, or the carriers on the root or its first 32 entries (a blob wins) */
+static enum lklfuse_xscheme lklfuse_volume_xscheme(void)
+{
+	static const char *const dirs[] = { "/.AppleDB", "/.AppleDouble", "/.AppleDesktop" };
+	unsigned long long b[512];
+	char path[LKLFUSE_PATH_MAX];
+	struct lkl_stat st;
+	long fd, n, off;
+	int i, s, seen = 0, fruit;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < 3; i++)
+		if (lkl_sys_lstat(dirs[i], &st) == 0 && LKL_S_ISDIR(st.st_mode))
+			return XS_NETATALK;
+	s = lklfuse_xmarks("/", 1);
+	if (s == XS_NETATALK)
+		return XS_NETATALK;
+	fruit = s == XS_FRUIT_STREAM;
+	fd = lkl_sys_open("/", LKL_O_RDONLY | LKL_O_DIRECTORY, 0);
+	while (fd >= 0 && seen < 32 && (n = lkl_sys_getdents64(fd, (void *)b, sizeof(b))) > 0) {
+		for (off = 0; off < n && seen < 32; ) {
+			struct lkl_linux_dirent64 *de = (void *)((char *)b + off);
+
+			off += de->d_reclen;
+			if (strcmp(de->d_name, ".") == 0 || strcmp(de->d_name, "..") == 0)
+				continue;
+			seen++;
+			snprintf(path, sizeof(path), "/%s", de->d_name);
+			s = lklfuse_xmarks(path, 1);
+			if (s == XS_NETATALK) {
+				lkl_sys_close(fd);
+				return XS_NETATALK;
+			}
+			fruit |= s == XS_FRUIT_STREAM;
+		}
+	}
+	if (fd >= 0)
+		lkl_sys_close(fd);
+	return fruit ? XS_FRUIT_STREAM : XS_OURS;
+}
+
+/* a stream's data VAL, written as streams_xattr writes it: with one more byte, 0 */
+static long lklfuse_xstream_put(const char *path, const char *name, const char *val, size_t size, int flags)
+{
+	char *v = malloc(size + 1);
+	long ret;
+
+	if (!v)
+		return -LKL_ENOMEM;
+	memcpy(v, val, size);
+	v[size] = 0;
+	ret = lkl_sys_setxattr(path, name, v, size + 1, flags);
+	free(v);
+	return ret;
+}
